+## Opt in to set-based enqueue on PostgreSQL 17
+
+Run `Jobs.migrate` as the Jobs owner, then apply the current Jobs role grants
+if your producer uses a scoped role. Start the producer with
+`MESH_JOBS_SET_BASED_ENQUEUE=1` to test the set-based writer. The same setting
+covers `Jobs.enqueue` and `Jobs.enqueue_in`. The PostgreSQL functions install
+alongside the existing scalar function, so older binaries can keep writing
+to the same namespace.
+
+Batches of 16 to 128 independent specs can use the fast path on the stock
+PostgreSQL 17 Jobs layout in a READ COMMITTED transaction. A custom table
+layout, rule, trigger, or row-security policy selects the ordered writer.
+The same fallback applies to existing or duplicate request keys and to
+batches with uniqueness or replacement policies. All writes remain under
+the namespace fence and the caller's transaction. After transport loss,
+use the original request keys to resolve the enqueue outcome.
+
